 R6 Feedback and Recovery: This dimension applies when handling an existing error, contradiction, or invalid result, or when repeating an earlier query or operation. Assign N for normal first-time progress or the first occurrence of an error. Assign P for fixing an earlier error or supplying necessary additional information, even if an independent new error occurs. Fixing an execution problem does not cancel task-related errors under R3-R5. Assign F for ignoring feedback, repeating known errors, or repeating queries without new information or a need for verification. Compare the current state with what was actually executed: refreshing state and skipping already completed work can be valid recovery. Do not assign F solely because code is identical or a potential defect was not triggered. After a compound write fails, assign F for repeating writes that may cause conflicts or duplicate side effects without checking for partial success.
 
